# ============================================================
# Client Workspace — Environment Variables
# ============================================================
#
# INSTRUCTIONS:
# 1. Copy this file: cp .env.example .env
# 2. Fill in your real values from 1Password (or your password manager)
# 3. NEVER commit the .env file — it's blocked by .gitignore
# 4. Claude Code CANNOT read .env files — this is a security feature
#
# !! CRITICAL — READ THIS !!
# This is your ONE core .env. Every key in it is labeled with five lines:
# Purpose, Phase, Get it from, Cost and Owner (see the layout below).
# Use your OWN key wherever the provider allows it, even when someone
# else pays. A key may live in exactly four places: the provider account
# that issued it → your password manager → this .env file → and, for a
# deployed app that needs it, that host's encrypted settings (for example
# a Vercel variable marked Sensitive). NOWHERE ELSE. Not Slack. Not email.
# Not Claude chat. Not a Google Doc. Not a repository, this AIOS included.
# If a key must be shared, the account owner shares it through the
# password manager with named people, and 00_AIOS/systems/key_registry.md
# records who holds it.
# If a key appears outside those four places, REVOKE IT IMMEDIATELY and
# make a new one.
# Spend: an alert only notifies; an enforced limit stops calls (it can lag,
# and it may cover a key, a project or the whole organization). Write on
# each Cost line which one is on.
# The key registry lists every key's name and purpose, never a value.
# Run /env_keys in Claude Code to add, share or retire a key.
# ============================================================

# --- Claude API ---------------------------------------------
# Purpose: Claude through the API, only for API billing or the CI reviewer.
#          A Claude subscription needs no key here.
# Phase: optional
# Get it from: the Anthropic Console, API keys page, signed in as yourself
# Cost: billed per use. Before first use: an alert, plus an enforced limit
#       where the Console offers one. Write which is on, and its scope.
# Owner: your account (write who pays if it isn't you)
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- OpenAI API ---------------------------------------------
# Purpose: embeddings or Whisper transcription only
# Phase: optional
# Get it from: the OpenAI platform, API keys page, signed in as yourself
# Cost: billed per use. Before first use: an alert, plus an enforced limit
#       where its billing settings offer one. Write which is on, and its scope.
# Owner: your account (write who pays if it isn't you)
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# --- FF Core Bridge -----------------------------------------
# Purpose: an FF Intelligence capability your organization is entitled to use
# Phase: optional
# Get it from: issued by Funnel Futurist with that entitlement
# Cost: set by your organization's agreement with Funnel Futurist
# Owner: your organization
# FF_CORE_KEY=

# --- Google Workspace API -----------------------------------
# Purpose: the OAuth client ID, for connecting Google Workspace via its API
# Phase: optional
# Get it from: Google Cloud Console, APIs & Services, Credentials (OAuth client)
# Cost: no charge to create; check the pricing of each Google API you enable
# Owner: the Google account that owns the Cloud project
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# Purpose: the OAuth client secret that pairs with the client ID
# Phase: optional
# Get it from: the same OAuth client in Google Cloud Console
# Cost: no charge to create; check the pricing of each Google API you enable
# Owner: the Google account that owns the Cloud project
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Purpose: the refresh token that keeps the API connection signed in
# Phase: optional
# Get it from: authorizing the OAuth client once with your Google account
# Cost: no charge to create; check the pricing of each Google API you enable
# Owner: the Google account that authorized it
# GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN=
